.TH PRINTF 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
printf \- format and print data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printf
\fIFORMAT\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print FORMAT with each ARGUMENT substituted for the next \fB%s\fR/\fB%d\fR/\fB%x\fR conversion, and \fB\\n\fR/\fB\\t\fR/\fB\\\\\fR escapes expanded. Supports \fB%%\fR for a literal percent sign.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Width/precision specifiers (e.g. \fB%5d\fR) and \fB%f\fR are not supported -- see mitos-utils-compat(7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 if FORMAT is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
